mpany offers grocery, meat, produce, dairy, deli, seafood, prepared food, bakery, and frozen food products. It also provides non-food products, including health and beauty care, general merchandise, liquor, and pharmacy products. The company offers its products under the Wholesome Pantry, Bowl & Basket, Paperbird, and Fairway and Gourmet Garage brands. It operates its supermarkets under the ShopRite and Fairway banners, and specialty markets under the Gourmet Garage banner; and online stores through shoprite.com, fairwaymarket.com, and gourmetgarage.com websites, as well as ShopRite app, Fairway app, and Gourmet Garage app. Village Super Market, Inc. was founded in 1937 and is based in Springfield, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John J. Sumas | CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Defensive peers. Each employee generates $26K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Village Super Market, Inc. is a small-cap consumer defensive business with a $599M market cap on $2.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 7% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 28%.","The business throws off $55M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.07\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 19\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 14% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 33% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 22% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","23 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above 